    {
      "heading": "About the pronunciations",
      "text": [
        "Pronunciations follow standard ijekavian Serbo-Croatian (as used in Croatia, Bosnia and Montenegro), written as exact (bracketed) IPA. Spelling is phonetic: every letter is pronounced, always the same way. ˈ marks the stressed syllable (one-syllable words are always stressed, so they are not marked), and its vowel carries one of four pitch accents: a circumflex (â) for a falling pitch and a caron (ǎ) for a rising one, each short or long (ː). Long vowels after the stress are marked ː too. Falling accents only occur on the first syllable; rising ones never on the last."
      ]
    },
